From: Ali Erdinc Koroglu <ali.koroglu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:04:20 +0300
Subject: build: report the CBOR backend actually used in Requires.private

Commit "Enable libcbor fallback when QCBOR is unavailable" (PR #23) made
the CBOR backend selectable at configure time, but pc_req_private stayed
hardcoded to qcbor. A build that falls back to libcbor therefore installs
a qcomtee.pc declaring a private dependency on a module that is not
present, which breaks static linking and dependency generation for
downstream consumers.

Set pc_req_private from QCBOR_FOUND. The libcbor pkg-config module is
named libcbor, not cbor.

Signed-off-by: Ali Erdinc Koroglu <ali.koroglu@oss.qualcomm.com>

Origin: https://github.com/qualcomm/quic-teec/pull/30/commits/07c4a35a42093af96a5352ec4786ce686f6bf42e
Forwarded: https://github.com/qualcomm/quic-teec/pull/30
Last-Update: 2026-10-07
---
 libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt b/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
index bc80a52..adaef66 100644
--- a/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -29,7 +29,12 @@ add_library(qcomtee ${SRC})
 
 # ''Library pkg-config file and version''.
 
-set(pc_req_private qcbor)
+if(QCBOR_FOUND)
+	set(pc_req_private qcbor)
+else()
+	set(pc_req_private libcbor)
+endif()
+
 set(libqcomteetgt qcomtee)
 
 configure_file(qcomtee.pc.in qcomtee.pc @ONLY)

